var DOC_PAGES = {
  "readme": {
    id: "readme",
    title: "README",
    file: "README.md",
    blurb: "Overview, quick start, centering gotcha",
    markdown: "# ytea\n\n**ytea** lets you build websites with two tiny dialects that still use **real** HTML, CSS, and JavaScript words.\n\n- `#UI//` — how it looks (layout + style)\n- `#Y//` — what it does (logic)\n\nytea only changes the **shape** of the code (indent, dots, `@ids`). It never invents fake property names. If MDN has it, you can type it.\n\nOpen `index.html` in a browser — no build step, no install.\n\n---\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Open `index.html` (double-click or any local server).\n2. Edit `main.ytea` (`#UI//`) and `logic.ytea` (`#Y//`).\n3. Press **Compile** (`Ctrl/Cmd+S`) or **Run** (`Ctrl/Cmd+Enter`).\n4. Export a single `*.html` file when you are happy.\n\n### Tiny example\n\n**main.ytea**\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"app\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .display(flex)\n  .align-items(center)\n  .justify-content(center)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n\n  button(id=\"go\") \"Click me\"\n    .padding(12px 18px)\n    .border-radius(8px)\n    .cursor(pointer)\n```\n\n**logic.ytea**\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nvar n = 0\n\non click @go\n  n += 1\n  set text of @go to \"Clicked \" + n\n```\n\n---\n\n## Mental model\n\n| File header | Role | Compiles to |\n|-------------|------|-------------|\n| `#UI//` | Structure + CSS | HTML + inline styles |\n| `#Y//` | Behavior | JavaScript |\n\n- Indentation = nesting (UI children, Y blocks).\n- `.property(value)` = real CSS (`background`, `display`, `align-items`, …).\n- `@myId` = `document.getElementById('myId')`.\n- Comments: `// like this`.\n\n---\n\n## Docs\n\n| Doc | What’s inside |\n|-----|----------------|\n| [docs/ui-language.md](docs/ui-language.md) | `#UI//` tags, attributes, CSS modifiers, centering |\n| [docs/y-language.md](docs/y-language.md) | Full `#Y//` reference (events, loops, helpers) |\n| [docs/examples.md](docs/examples.md) | Copy-paste patterns |\n| [docs/compiler.md](docs/compiler.md) | How compile / preview / export work |\n| [docs/cheatsheet.md](docs/cheatsheet.md) | One-page cheat sheet |\n\nIn the app, open **`?`** to read this README, then click **Docs** for the language reference pages.\n\n---\n\n## Centering (common gotcha)\n\nThis does **not** center content:\n\n```ytea\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .align-items(center)\n  h1 \"test\"\n```\n\n`align-items` only works on a **flex** or **grid** container. The compiler correctly emits `align-items: center;` — CSS simply ignores it without `display: flex` / `grid`.\n\nDo this instead:\n\n```ytea\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .display(flex)\n  .flex-direction(column)\n  .align-items(center)\n  .justify-content(center)\n  h1 \"test\"\n```\n\n- `align-items` → cross axis (row → vertical, column → horizontal)\n- `justify-content` → main axis\n- `min-height(100vh)` → give the box the full viewport so centering is visible\n\nNot a compiler bug — same rule as plain CSS.\n\n---\n\n## Editor shortcuts\n\n| Shortcut | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| `Ctrl/Cmd + S` | Compile |\n| `Ctrl/Cmd + Enter` | Run preview popup |\n| `Tab` / `Enter` | Accept autocomplete |\n| `↑` `↓` | Move in autocomplete |\n| `Ctrl/Cmd + Space` | Open autocomplete |\n| `Esc` | Close autocomplete |\n| `Tab` (no menu) | Insert 2 spaces |\n| `Enter` | New line + smart indent |\n\nAutocomplete loads HTML tags + CSS properties from official catalogs (MDN data / html-tags), with an offline fallback.\n\n---\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\nytea/\n├── index.html      # App shell\n├── app.js          # Editor, autocomplete, compilers\n├── style.css       # App UI\n├── README.md\n└── docs/           # Language docs\n```\n\nWorkspaces and files are stored in the browser (`localStorage`). Export writes a standalone HTML file.\n\n---\n\n## Philosophy\n\n1. **Real names** — `background`, not `bg`. `textContent`, not a made-up API.\n2. **Readable shape** — indent instead of braces where it helps; still JS underneath.\n3. **Escape hatch** — any normal JavaScript still works in `#Y//`.\n4. **One HTML out** — compile merges all `#UI//` + `#Y//` files into one page.\n\n---\n\n## License\n\nUse freely for learning and building."
  },
  "ui-language": {
    id: "ui-language",
    title: "#UI// language",
    file: "docs/ui-language.md",
    blurb: "Tags, CSS modifiers, nesting, centering",
    markdown: "# `#UI//` — how it looks\n\nA UI file always starts with:\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\n```\n\nEverything after that is structure (HTML tags) and style (CSS modifiers).\n\n---\n\n## Elements\n\n```ytea\ntag\ntag \"text content\"\ntag(id=\"box\" class=\"card\") \"Hello\"\n```\n\n- Tag names are **real HTML**: `div`, `button`, `input`, `img`, `a`, …\n- Attributes go in `(…)` with normal HTML syntax: `id=\"…\"`, `type=\"text\"`, `href=\"…\"`.\n- Optional text after the tag becomes the element’s text content.\n\n### Void tags\n\nTags that cannot have children (`img`, `input`, `br`, `hr`, …) still accept indented `.styles()`:\n\n```ytea\nimg(src=\"photo.jpg\" alt=\"A photo\")\n  .width(240px)\n  .border-radius(12px)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Nesting\n\nIndentation = parent / child:\n\n```ytea\ndiv(id=\"card\")\n  h1 \"Title\"\n  p \"Body text\"\n  div\n    button(id=\"ok\") \"OK\"\n    button(id=\"no\") \"Cancel\"\n```\n\nUse **2 spaces** per level (the editor inserts them on Tab / Enter).\n\n---\n\n## CSS modifiers\n\nUnder an element, lines that start with `.` are CSS:\n\n```ytea\ndiv(id=\"hero\")\n  .display(flex)\n  .padding(24px)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Name = **real CSS property** (`background-color`, `align-items`, `font-size`, …).\n- Value = whatever CSS accepts (`16px`, `#3ecf6a`, `center`, `1fr 1fr`, …).\n- Compiles to inline `style=\"…\"`.\n\n```ytea\n.padding(16px)\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```html\nstyle=\"padding: 16px;\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Centering content\n\n`align-items` and `justify-content` only work when the element is a flex or grid container.\n\n### Full-page center\n\n```ytea\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .display(flex)\n  .flex-direction(column)\n  .align-items(center)\n  .justify-content(center)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n\n  h1 \"Centered\"\n```\n\n| Property | Job |\n|----------|-----|\n| `display(flex)` | Turns on flex layout (required) |\n| `flex-direction(column)` | Stack children vertically |\n| `align-items(center)` | Center on the cross axis |\n| `justify-content(center)` | Center on the main axis |\n| `min-height(100vh)` | Fill the viewport so centering is visible |\n\n### Horizontal row of buttons\n\n```ytea\ndiv\n  .display(flex)\n  .gap(10px)\n  .justify-content(center)\n\n  button(id=\"a\") \"A\"\n  button(id=\"b\") \"B\"\n```\n\n### Text-only center\n\nFor a single line of text you can also use:\n\n```ytea\np \"Hello\"\n  .text-align(center)\n```\n\nThat does **not** replace flex centering for blocks.\n\n---\n\n## Linking to `#Y//`\n\nGive interactive elements an `id`. Logic files refer to them with `@id`:\n\n```ytea\nbutton(id=\"save\") \"Save\"\ninput(id=\"name\" type=\"text\")\n```\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\non click @save\n  log value of @name\n```\n\n---\n\n## Comments & raw HTML\n\n```ytea\n// This line is ignored\n<div class=\"escape\">raw HTML if you need it</div>\n```\n\nRaw `<…>` lines are copied through as-is (escape hatch).\n\n---\n\n## Tips\n\n1. Prefer real CSS names — autocomplete lists MDN properties.\n2. Style the parent for layout; style children for look.\n3. One visual job per block keeps files readable.\n4. If a CSS property “does nothing”, check whether it needs a companion (`display`, `position`, width/height, etc.) — same as the browser."
  },
  "y-language": {
    id: "y-language",
    title: "#Y// language",
    file: "docs/y-language.md",
    blurb: "Events, loops, helpers, full reference",
    markdown: "# `#Y//` — what it does\n\nA logic file always starts with:\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\n```\n\nLines compile to JavaScript. Friendly ytea words become normal JS; anything else is passed through (with `@id` → `getElementById`).\n\n---\n\n## Variables & functions\n\n```ytea\nvar count = 0\nvar name = \"ytea\"\nvar items = [1, 2, 3]\n\nfunc greet(who)\n  log \"Hello \" + who\n\ngreet(\"Bubi\")\n```\n\n| ytea | JavaScript |\n|------|------------|\n| `var x = 1` | `let x = 1;` |\n| `func name(a, b)` + indent | `function name(a, b) { … }` |\n| `return value` | `return value;` |\n\n---\n\n## Talking to the UI (`@id`)\n\n`@btn` means the element with `id=\"btn\"`.\n\n```ytea\n@btn.textContent = \"Hi\"          // still valid JS\nset text of @btn to \"Hi\"         // same idea, friendlier\nlog text of @btn\nlog value of @email\n```\n\n| Expression | Becomes |\n|------------|---------|\n| `@id` | `document.getElementById('id')` |\n| `text of @id` | `….textContent` |\n| `value of @id` | `….value` |\n\n---\n\n## Events\n\nIndented lines under an event run when it fires. Inside handlers you get `event`.\n\n```ytea\non click @go\n  log \"clicked\"\n\non input @email\n  log value of @email\n\non change @select\n  log value of @select\n\non submit @form\n  event.preventDefault()\n  log \"submitted\"\n\non mouseenter @card\n  add class \"hover\" to @card\n\non mouseleave @card\n  remove class \"hover\" from @card\n\non keydown @field\n  log event.key\n\non key \"Enter\" @field\n  say \"You pressed Enter\"\n\nonce click @start\n  log \"only the first click\"\n\non load\n  log \"page ready\"\n```\n\nAliases for page ready: `on load`, `when ready`, `when load`.\n\n| Form | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `on EVENT @id` | `addEventListener('EVENT', …)` |\n| `on key \"X\" @id` | keydown, only if `event.key === \"X\"` |\n| `once EVENT @id` | listener with `{ once: true }` |\n| `on load` | `DOMContentLoaded` on `window` |\n\nAny DOM event name works (`click`, `dblclick`, `focus`, `blur`, `scroll`, …).\n\n---\n\n## Conditions\n\n```ytea\nif count > 10\n  say \"big\"\nelse if count > 0\n  say \"ok\"\nelse\n  say \"empty\"\n\nunless count == 0\n  log \"not zero\"\n```\n\n| ytea | JS |\n|------|----|\n| `if cond` | `if (cond) { }` |\n| `else if cond` | `else if (cond) { }` |\n| `else` | `else { }` |\n| `unless cond` | `if (!(cond)) { }` |\n\n---\n\n## Loops\n\n```ytea\nrepeat 5\n  log i\n\nfor item in items\n  log item\n\neach item in items\n  log item\n\nwhile count < 10\n  count += 1\n\nuntil ready\n  // keep going until ready is true\n  stop\n\nrepeat 10\n  if i == 3\n    skip\n  if i == 8\n    stop\n  log i\n```\n\n| ytea | JS |\n|------|----|\n| `repeat N` | `for (let i = 0; i < N; i++)` — use `i` inside |\n| `for x in list` / `each x in list` | `for (const x of list)` |\n| `while cond` | `while (cond)` |\n| `until cond` | `while (!(cond))` |\n| `stop` | `break` |\n| `skip` | `continue` |\n\n---\n\n## Time\n\n```ytea\nwait 1000\n  log \"1 second later\"\n\nevery 2000\n  log \"tick\"\n```\n\n| ytea | JS |\n|------|----|\n| `wait ms` + indent | `setTimeout(() => { … }, ms)` |\n| `every ms` + indent | `setInterval(() => { … }, ms)` |\n\nValues can be numbers or expressions: `wait delay`, `every 500 * 2`.\n\n---\n\n## Show, hide, focus, clear\n\n```ytea\nshow @panel\nhide @panel\ntoggle @panel\nfocus @email\nclear @email\nenable @save\ndisable @save\n```\n\n| ytea | Effect |\n|------|--------|\n| `show @id` | clear `display` (visible again) |\n| `hide @id` | `display = 'none'` |\n| `toggle @id` | flip visible / hidden |\n| `focus @id` | `.focus()` |\n| `clear @id` | empty `.value` or `.textContent` |\n| `enable @id` | `disabled = false` |\n| `disable @id` | `disabled = true` |\n\n---\n\n## Classes & styles\n\n```ytea\nadd class \"active\" to @tab\nremove class \"active\" from @tab\ntoggle class \"open\" on @menu\n\nset text of @title to \"Hello\"\nset value of @email to \"a@b.c\"\nset style color of @title to \"#3ecf6a\"\nset style background-color of @box to \"#151c18\"\nappend \"!\" to @title\n```\n\nCSS property names in `set style …` may use dashes; they become camelCase in JS (`background-color` → `backgroundColor`).\n\n---\n\n## Log, say, ask\n\n```ytea\nlog \"debug\" + count\nsay \"Saved!\"\nvar name = ask \"Your name?\"\nask \"Just a prompt\"\n```\n\n| ytea | JS |\n|------|----|\n| `log …` | `console.log(…)` |\n| `say …` | `alert(…)` |\n| `ask …` | `prompt(…)` |\n| `var x = ask \"…\"` | `let x = prompt(\"…\")` |\n\n---\n\n## Errors\n\n```ytea\ntry\n  JSON.parse(raw)\ncatch err\n  log err\n  say \"Bad JSON\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Escape hatch: real JavaScript\n\nAnything that is not a ytea keyword line is emitted as JS (`;` added if needed), with `@id` expanded:\n\n```ytea\nfetch(\"/api/hi\").then((r) => r.json()).then((data) => {\n  @out.textContent = data.message\n})\n\nlocalStorage.setItem(\"n\", count)\ncount = Number(localStorage.getItem(\"n\")) || 0\n```\n\nYou can mix MDN APIs freely: `Math`, `JSON`, `Date`, `fetch`, `classList`, …\n\n---\n\n## Compile map (summary)\n\n| ytea | JavaScript |\n|------|------------|\n| `on click @a` | `getElementById('a').addEventListener('click', (event) => {` |\n| `once click @a` | same + `{ once: true }` |\n| `on key \"Enter\" @a` | keydown + `if (event.key !== \"Enter\") return;` |\n| `on load` | `window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {` |\n| `wait 1000` | `setTimeout(() => { … }, 1000)` |\n| `every 1000` | `setInterval(() => { … }, 1000)` |\n| `show` / `hide` / `toggle` `@a` | display helpers |\n| `set text of @a to x` | `….textContent = x` |\n| `stop` / `skip` | `break` / `continue` |\n| `unless c` | `if (!(c))` |\n| `until c` | `while (!(c))` |\n\nFull examples: [examples.md](examples.md)."
  },
  "examples": {
    id: "examples",
    title: "Examples",
    file: "docs/examples.md",
    blurb: "Copy-paste patterns",
    markdown: "# Examples\n\nCopy these into `*.ytea` files in the editor.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Centered hello\n\n**main.ytea**\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .display(flex)\n  .align-items(center)\n  .justify-content(center)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n  .font-family(system-ui, sans-serif)\n\n  h1 \"Hello ytea\"\n    .margin(0)\n    .font-size(42px)\n```\n\n**logic.ytea**\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\non load\n  log \"ready\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Counter (UI + Y helpers)\n\n**main.ytea** — same idea as the default project: a card with two buttons (`btnCount`, `btnReset`).\n\n**logic.ytea**\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nvar count = 0\n\non click @btnCount\n  count += 1\n  set text of @btnCount to \"Count: \" + count\n\non click @btnReset\n  count = 0\n  set text of @btnCount to \"Count: 0\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Show / hide a panel\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"app\")\n  .padding(24px)\n\n  button(id=\"toggle\") \"Toggle panel\"\n  div(id=\"panel\") \"Secret panel\"\n    .margin-top(12px)\n    .padding(16px)\n    .background(#1a231e)\n```\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nhide @panel\n\non click @toggle\n  toggle @panel\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Form: Enter key + ask\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv\n  .padding(24px)\n  .display(flex)\n  .gap(8px)\n\n  input(id=\"name\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Your name\")\n  button(id=\"ok\") \"OK\"\n  p(id=\"out\") \"\"\n```\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nfunc greet()\n  var n = value of @name\n  if n == \"\"\n    n = ask \"Your name?\"\n  set text of @out to \"Hello, \" + n\n  clear @name\n  focus @name\n\non click @ok\n  greet()\n\non key \"Enter\" @name\n  greet()\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Timer with wait / every\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nvar ticks = 0\n\non click @start\n  set text of @status to \"Starting…\"\n  wait 1000\n    set text of @status to \"Go!\"\n  every 1000\n    ticks += 1\n    set text of @status to \"Tick \" + ticks\n    if ticks >= 5\n      stop\n```\n\n> Note: `stop` only breaks a `repeat` / `for` / `while` / `until` loop. To cancel `every`, keep the interval id in a `var` and use real JS `clearInterval(id)` (escape hatch), or reload the preview.\n\nSafer interval pattern with JS escape hatch:\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nvar timer = null\nvar ticks = 0\n\non click @start\n  if timer != null\n    clearInterval(timer)\n  ticks = 0\n  timer = setInterval(() => {\n    ticks += 1\n    @status.textContent = \"Tick \" + ticks\n    if (ticks >= 5) clearInterval(timer)\n  }, 1000)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. List rendering\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\nul(id=\"list\")\nbutton(id=\"add\") \"Add item\"\n```\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\nvar items = [\"Tea\", \"Milk\", \"Honey\"]\n\nfunc render()\n  clear @list\n  for item in items\n    @list.innerHTML += \"<li>\" + item + \"</li>\"\n\non load\n  render()\n\non click @add\n  var next = ask \"New item?\"\n  unless next == null\n    unless next == \"\"\n      items.push(next)\n      render()\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Theme toggle with classes\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"page\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .padding(32px)\n  .background(#f3faf5)\n  .color(#0c100e)\n\n  button(id=\"theme\") \"Dark mode\"\n  p(id=\"hint\") \"Click to flip theme\"\n```\n\n```ytea\n#Y//\non click @theme\n  toggle class \"dark\" on @page\n  if @page.classList.contains(\"dark\")\n    set style background of @page to \"#0c100e\"\n    set style color of @page to \"#f3faf5\"\n    set text of @theme to \"Light mode\"\n  else\n    set style background of @page to \"#f3faf5\"\n    set style color of @page to \"#0c100e\"\n    set text of @theme to \"Dark mode\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Why centering failed (before / after)\n\n**Before (looks left-aligned):**\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .padding(32px)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n  .align-items(center)\n  h1 \"test\"\n```\n\nCompiles to `align-items: center` **without** `display: flex` → browser ignores it.\n\n**After:**\n\n```ytea\n#UI//\ndiv(id=\"root\")\n  .min-height(100vh)\n  .display(flex)\n  .flex-direction(column)\n  .align-items(center)\n  .justify-content(center)\n  .padding(32px)\n  .background(#0c100e)\n  .color(#f3faf5)\n  h1 \"test\"\n```"
  },
  "compiler": {
    id: "compiler",
    title: "Compiler",
    file: "docs/compiler.md",
    blurb: "Compile, preview, export, storage",
    markdown: "# Compiler & app workflow\n\nytea runs entirely in the browser. `app.js` owns editing, autocomplete, compilation, assets, and ZenoPack export.\n\n---\n\n## What Compile does\n\n1. Walks every `.ytea` file in the active project (not assets).\n2. Files starting with `#Y//` → `restructureYToJS`.\n3. Everything else (usually `#UI//`) → `restructureUIToHTML`.\n4. Wraps the result in a full HTML document (`index.html` for the pack):\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>…title + base CSS…</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- each UI file -->\n  …\n\n  <script>\n    // --- each Y file ---\n    …\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nOrder = file order in the project. Put structure first, logic second (default template already does this).\n\n---\n\n## Assets\n\nUnder **Assets** you can add any files or whole folders (no type filter). Paths keep their folder structure (e.g. `images/logo.png`). Assets are stored with the project and packed into the export as-is.\n\nReference them from `#UI//` with normal paths, e.g. `img(src=\"images/logo.png\")`.\n\n---\n\n## Preview & export\n\n| Action | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| **Compile** | Builds the HTML document + status |\n| **Run** | Opens a popup with the ZenoPack standalone HTML (compiled site + assets) |\n| **Export** | Packs compiled `index.html` + all assets into a `.zenopack`, then embeds that into a standalone `.html` download |\n\nShortcuts: `Ctrl/Cmd+S` compile · `Ctrl/Cmd+Enter` run.\n\n---\n\n## Storage\n\nProjects live in `localStorage`:\n\n- `ytea_pure_workspaces_v4` — all workspaces / files / assets\n- `ytea_pure_active_ws_v4` — last active project\n- `ytea_official_catalog_v1` — cached HTML/CSS autocomplete catalogs\n\nClearing site data resets projects to the default demo. Very large assets may hit browser storage limits.\n\n---\n\n## Autocomplete catalogs\n\nOn load, ytea fetches:\n\n- MDN CSS properties (`mdn-data`)\n- HTML tag list (`html-tags`)\n\nIf offline, a small fallback list is used. Type `.` in `#UI//` for CSS, tag names for HTML, `@` in `#Y//` for your element ids.\n\n---\n\n## Design rules of the compilers\n\n1. **UI** — no invented CSS; `.foo(bar)` → `foo: bar;`.\n2. **Y** — keyword lines become JS blocks; unknown lines pass through as statements.\n3. **`@id`** — always `document.getElementById('id')` (also inside strings? No — strings are preserved).\n4. **Indent** — closes blocks when indentation goes back out.\n\n---\n\n## Debugging tips\n\n1. Use **Run** and the browser console in the preview popup (`log …` helps).\n2. If a CSS rule “does nothing”, check the compiled styles — usually a missing companion property (e.g. `display:flex` for `align-items`).\n3. If `@id` is `null`, the id is missing in a `#UI//` file or the script runs before the element (keep UI above the script — default template is fine).\n4. If an asset does not load in Run/Export, check the path matches the Assets tree exactly.\n"
  },
  "cheatsheet": {
    id: "cheatsheet",
    title: "Cheat sheet",
    file: "docs/cheatsheet.md",
    blurb: "One-page reference",
    markdown: "# ytea cheat sheet\n\n## Headers\n\n```\n#UI//     how it looks\n#Y//      what it does\n```\n\n## `#UI//`\n\n```\ndiv(id=\"box\")\n  .display(flex)\n  .padding(16px)\n  h1 \"Title\"\n  button(id=\"go\") \"Go\"\n```\n\n| Want | Write |\n|------|--------|\n| Nest | indent 2 spaces |\n| Style | `.css-property(value)` |\n| Center page | `.min-height(100vh)` + `.display(flex)` + `.align-items(center)` + `.justify-content(center)` |\n| Comment | `// …` |\n\n`align-items` **needs** `display(flex)` or `display(grid)`.\n\n## `#Y//` — core\n\n```\nvar n = 0\nfunc hi(name)\n  log name\n\non click @go\n  n += 1\n  set text of @go to \"n=\" + n\n```\n\n## `#Y//` — events\n\n```\non click @id\non input @id\non change @id\non submit @id\non keydown @id\non key \"Enter\" @id\non mouseenter @id\non mouseleave @id\nonce click @id\non load\n```\n\n## `#Y//` — control\n\n```\nif / else if / else / unless\nrepeat N\nfor x in list   ·  each x in list\nwhile cond      ·  until cond\ntry / catch err\nstop  (= break) ·  skip (= continue)\nwait ms         ·  every ms\n```\n\n## `#Y//` — DOM helpers\n\n```\nshow @id · hide @id · toggle @id\nfocus @id · clear @id\nenable @id · disable @id\nadd class \"x\" to @id\nremove class \"x\" from @id\ntoggle class \"x\" on @id\nset text of @id to …\nset value of @id to …\nset style color of @id to …\nappend \"!\" to @id\ntext of @id · value of @id\nlog … · say … · ask …\nvar x = ask \"…\"\n```\n\n## `#Y//` — refs\n\n```\n@myId          → getElementById('myId')\n@myId.prop     → still works (JS)\n```\n\n## Shortcuts\n\n| Key | Action |\n|-----|--------|\n| `Ctrl/Cmd+S` | Compile |\n| `Ctrl/Cmd+Enter` | Run |\n| `Ctrl+Space` | Autocomplete |\n| `Tab` / `Enter` | Accept hint |\n\n## Docs map\n\n- [UI language](ui-language.md)\n- [Y language](y-language.md)\n- [Examples](examples.md)\n- [Compiler](compiler.md)\n- [README](../README.md)"
  }
};
